{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3062","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3062","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3062\",\"parent_revision\":\"eb46fd075f34588e5fbe81c13d6527b952bfcb06\",\"root_revision\":\"102440addc9a419a63baa60a413099cc9290783896aaa5a06f9d270b240745d5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nPagination has no content identity. Page structures carry a page number and total, but nothing identifying which document they page. Across stateless invocations a caller cannot request \\\"the next page of what you just returned\\\" \u2014 every page request re-collects from the provider and re-parses.\\n\\nThis is also a correctness gap: if content changes between page requests, pages from two different versions can be returned as though they were one document.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:11:49.444303Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-20T09:24:48.111733Z \u2014 impact-analyst broadcast a scope-expanding finding (1b): backlog_view does not currently route through progressive_markdown's ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator at all (verified: zero references in backlog_core/server.py; backlog_view runs its own separate, duplicate pagination logic). Re-issuing RT-ICA with this as a new MISSING condition requiring a human scope decision before planning proceeds.</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: address paginated content by content identity\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Implement the content-identity-addressed control set (R8 of the markdown-consumption contract) so paginated/navigable responses are addressable and re-servable without re-collecting from source or redoing Generation, per ADR-3082-1's finalized design.\\nConditions:\\n1. content_id derivation rule (command + Generation output binding, not raw source or generated content alone) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Storage schema (content_id PK, source, command, content, stale marker, timestamps) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Storage location convention (state_root()/control-set.db, WAL mode) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Eviction/cleanup policy parameters (40MB soft target, LRU-by-size, periodic rate-limited hourly-to-daily sweep) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Which existing write paths across the codebase must trigger invalidation (marking a matching content_id stale) | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Where the Navigation stage currently lives in code (progressive_markdown package) and what wiring is needed to route through the new control set | Status: DERIVABLE\\n7. FileCache/GitHubContentCache boundary \u2014 confirmed unrelated to the control set, must not be conflated | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. task_status_hook.py's exact current location and shape (flagged by cross-session review as a future required invalidation-trigger caller) | Status: MISSING\\n9. Concurrent-writer hardening scope confirmed deferred to #3081, not blocking this item's baseline single-writer path | Status: AVAILABLE\\n10. Existing test patterns for backend/provider code in this plugin to follow | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 1\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T09:24:48.111754Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-20T21:12:38.790828Z \u2014 Repo owner decided both MISSING conditions: #3062's scope expands to include migrating backlog_view onto ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator, and artifact_read's content_id/hash/refresh parameter surface is part of #3062 (deeper artifact_read engine-routing work stays with #3078).</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: address paginated content by content identity\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Implement the content-identity-addressed control set (R8 of the markdown-consumption contract) so paginated/navigable responses are addressable and re-servable without re-collecting from source or redoing Generation, per ADR-3082-1's finalized design.\\nConditions:\\n1. content_id derivation rule (command + Generation output binding, not raw source or generated content alone) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Storage schema (content_id PK, source, command, content, stale marker, timestamps) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Storage location convention (state_root()/control-set.db, WAL mode) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Eviction/cleanup policy parameters (40MB soft target, LRU-by-size, periodic rate-limited hourly-to-daily sweep) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Which existing write paths across the codebase must trigger invalidation (marking a matching content_id stale) | Status: AVAILABLE (resolved by impact-analyst: backlog_core/server.py's mutating tools, sam_schema/server.py's sam_plan/sam_task write actions, task_status_hook.py)\\n6. Where the Navigation stage currently lives in code (progressive_markdown package) and what wiring is needed to route through the new control set | Status: AVAILABLE (resolved by technical-researcher: ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator.load() is the single chokepoint; control set sits between Collection and parse)\\n7. FileCache/GitHubContentCache boundary \u2014 confirmed unrelated to the control set, must not be conflated | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. task_status_hook.py's exact current location and shape | Status: AVAILABLE (resolved by technical-researcher: plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py, subprocess-isolated, calls _call_sam_fastmcp())\\n9. Concurrent-writer hardening scope confirmed deferred to #3081, not blocking this item's baseline single-writer path | Status: AVAILABLE\\n10. Existing test patterns for backend/provider code in this plugin to follow | Status: AVAILABLE (resolved by technical-researcher: test_dispatch_state.py is the direct precedent)\\n11. dh_paths.py state_root()/compute_slug() placement details | Status: AVAILABLE (resolved by technical-researcher; a pre-existing unrelated slug-computation drift was found and filed separately as #3091, not part of this item's scope)\\n12. Does backlog_view (the plugin's single most-called tool) actually route through progressive_markdown's ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator today, such that wiring content_id into the engine automatically backs live backlog_view traffic? | Status: MISSING \u2014 verified FALSE (impact-analyst confirmed zero references to ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator in backlog_core/server.py; backlog_view runs its own separate, duplicate pagination logic that component-architecture.md itself says is \\\"scheduled for deletion, not maintenance\\\" with no tracked migration issue). This is a scope decision, not a fact gap: does #3062 stay scoped to \\\"build the store + wire the engine\\\" (with the backlog_view-onto-engine migration filed as a separate follow-up item), or does #3062's scope expand to include migrating backlog_view onto ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator so the store actually backs live traffic on landing? Requires human decision.\\n13. Does artifact_read's parameter surface (content_id/hash, refresh) belong in #3062's scope, or is it fully deferred to #3078? | Status: MISSING \u2014 impact-analyst flagged this as ambiguous: #3078 tracks artifact_read's engine-routing generally, but the R8 parameter/response-shape addition itself may need to land as part of #3062's read-path work regardless of #3078's status. Requires human decision alongside condition 12.\\nAVAILABLE count: 11\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 2\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-20T21:12:38.790851Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: address paginated content by content identity\\nDate: 2026-08-20\\nGoal: Implement the content-identity-addressed control set (R8 of the markdown-consumption contract), migrate backlog_view and artifact_read's parameter surface onto it, so paginated/navigable responses across the plugin's two most-used read tools are addressable and re-servable without re-collecting from source or redoing Generation, per ADR-3082-1's finalized design.\\nConditions:\\n1. content_id derivation rule (command + Generation output binding, not raw source or generated content alone) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Storage schema (content_id PK, source, command, content, stale marker, timestamps) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Storage location convention (state_root()/control-set.db, WAL mode) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Eviction/cleanup policy parameters (40MB soft target, LRU-by-size, periodic rate-limited hourly-to-daily sweep) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. Which existing write paths across the codebase must trigger invalidation | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. Where the Navigation stage currently lives in code (progressive_markdown package) and what wiring is needed | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. FileCache/GitHubContentCache boundary \u2014 confirmed unrelated, must not be conflated | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. task_status_hook.py's exact current location and shape | Status: AVAILABLE\\n9. Concurrent-writer hardening scope confirmed deferred to #3081 | Status: AVAILABLE\\n10. Existing test patterns for backend/provider code in this plugin | Status: AVAILABLE\\n11. dh_paths.py state_root()/compute_slug() placement details (pre-existing unrelated drift filed separately as #3091) | Status: AVAILABLE\\n12. Scope decision: does #3062 include migrating backlog_view onto ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator? | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 DECIDED by repo owner: YES, #3062's scope expands to include this migration. backlog_view (backlog_core/server.py) must be migrated off its own duplicate pagination logic and onto ProgressiveMarkdownNavigator as part of this item, so the control set backs live traffic on landing, not just new code nothing calls yet.\\n13. Scope decision: does artifact_read's content_id/hash/refresh parameter surface belong in #3062? | Status: AVAILABLE \u2014 DECIDED by repo owner: YES, part of #3062. The deeper \\\"route artifact_read through the engine at all\\\" work (artifact_read currently bypasses the engine entirely, calling provider.get_content() directly